# Everything the build installs or generates for itself, so `COPY stack/... `
# never carries a host tree into the image:
#   - npm ci regenerates node_modules (the prisma client is generated in-stage);
#   - npx tsc / ng build regenerate dist;
#   - pip installs into the image.
# Runtime data (grabbytube.db, grabby-tracks.json, downloads, cookies) belongs
# under /data, not under /srv/stack, so it is ignored here even though the
# vendored trees still hold the files the old containers wrote in place.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.angular/
**/npm-debug.log*

# Secrets and host-only config: tracked files carry placeholders and read real
# values from the environment, so a .env must never reach the image (a baked
# secret survives every later rebuild of the .env bind-mount).
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.local

# Runtime state from the standalone deployments (the hub keeps its own copy of
# each under /data; migrate.py moves these in).
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
stack/grabbytube/grabby-tracks.json
stack/grabbytube/grabby-index.json
**/*.bak
stack/tunester/downloads/
stack/tunester/.nzb-cache/
stack/vault/data/
stack/drivepod/data/
stack/drivepod/cache/
stack/frogrock/dnas/

# VCS + editor noise: the vendored trees keep their own .gitignored shape, and
# `git` metadata would only bloat the build context.
**/.git/
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
.dockerignore
data/
*.tar
*.tar.gz
